---
// The phone menu button, minus upstream's <script>.
//
// Same markup, same place in the layout: the sidebar pane opens through
// Starlight's own `[aria-expanded=true] ~ .sidebar-pane` sibling selector, so
// the root element here has to keep that attribute and that position. The
// behaviour is mobile-menu-toggle.client.ts in the kb bundle — a classic
// script, so unlike the module chunk this override replaces, the menu opens on
// a downloaded folder too. An external module is CORS-blocked from file://,
// which leaves a phone reader on disk unable to open the navigation at all.
//
// The element is a div with data-kb-menu-button, deliberately NOT
// `<starlight-menu-button>`: upstream's script defines that custom element as
// an import side effect, and the TocTracking override records why keeping such
// a tag invites upstream's behaviour back (its CLAUDE.md).
//
// The open state is `data-kb-menu-open`, NOT the `aria-expanded` upstream put
// here. A bare <div> has the implicit role `generic`, which ARIA allows no
// `aria-expanded` on — so the attribute named a state no assistive technology
// would ever read, on all 32 pages, and `check-site-axe` reports it as a
// critical `aria-allowed-attr` violation. The inner <button> is the element
// that legitimately carries it, and always did. The one thing the root's copy
// was load-bearing for is upstream's `~ .sidebar-pane` sibling selector;
// mobile-menu-toggle.css restates that rule against the data hook.
//
// Overriding the component also drops its Astro-scoped styles from the
// bundle, which is why mobile-menu-toggle.css re-states them.
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
---

<div
  class="kb-menu-button print:hidden"
  data-kb-menu-button
  data-kb-menu-open="false"
  data-kb-skip
>
  <button
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-label={Astro.locals.t('menuButton.accessibleLabel')}
    aria-controls="starlight__sidebar"
    class="sl-flex md:sl-hidden"
  >
    <Icon name="bars" class="open-menu" />
    <Icon name="close" class="close-menu" />
  </button>
</div>
